WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.470
An ancient Hindu text, the Kena Upanishad,

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.570
makes a startling claim.

3
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:08.810
Brahman is that which
speech does not illumine,

4
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.940
but which illumines speech.

5
00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:15.030
And it adds: not this
which people worship here.

6
00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:20.160
Yet many Hindus worship a personal
God, who can be loved and prayed to.

7
00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:25.710
So can Brahman be beyond all words, and
still be a God that Hindus love and pray

8
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:26.880
to?

9
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:31.540
In this mission, you'll climb the ladder
from Brahman beyond qualities to Brahman

10
00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:35.430
as a personal God, and
meet three great schools.

11
00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:38.920
Then you'll put these beliefs
through philosophy's tests:

12
00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.280
are they reasonable,
meaningful and coherent?

13
00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:47.610
Your mission: find out how Brahman can
be beyond all words and still be loved

14
00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:48.590
and prayed to.
